Claim --- We have \theta = 60{\textopenbullet}.
Proof. The left-hand side is increasing in \theta and the right-hand side is decreasing in \theta, so
at most one value of \theta works. But we also have
4 sin 20{\textopenbullet}sin 40{\textopenbullet}cos 10{\textopenbullet}= 2 (cos 20{\textopenbullet}-cos 60{\textopenbullet}) cos 10{\textopenbullet}
= 2 cos 20{\textopenbullet}cos 10{\textopenbullet}+ sin 80{\textopenbullet}
= (cos 30{\textopenbullet}-cos 10{\textopenbullet}) + sin 80{\textopenbullet}= cos 30{\textopenbullet}
as desired.
